        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 80-year-old female admitted on 15/04/2008 with an acute exacerbation of her known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray was performed excluding pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Spirometry supported obstructive ventilatory impairment consistent with severe COPD. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Her condition improved satisfactorily and she was discharged on 16/04/2008 in stable condition. I recommend continuation of her inhaled maintenance therapy and close follow-up in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
